+unchanged:
+- An ordinary pane close retires the clone through the existing undoable retirement on the next observation step; nothing un-retires it without a graph undo or resurrection.
+- threads_seat is write-once except for seat succession of a final-retired seat; at most one non-retired clone holds a seat (B1 1:1).
+- There is no separate "retired-final" clone state; graph clone retirement stays undoable until purge.
+- Participation is keyed to threads_seat, survives agent exit with the pane open (B8), and is not released on clone retirement.
+- The key env var is emitted only for a clone whose reservation is recorded; no key is emitted before D1.
+- HERDR_GRAPH_CLONE is still set on every agent start and on panes the graph creates.
+- The resume driver never launches into a pane with an agent, applies the 90 s incarnation grace after a restart, and is the only launcher for the clones it covers.
+- Threads unreachable changes no binding, writes no seat or intent, and launches nothing that depends on a threads answer.
+- Gating stays delivery order: the matcher deletion and fresh-agent path wait on D1, unretire and finalize on D2; no runtime capability switches.
+- Undo never adopts the caller's pane.
+- Tabs and workspaces match by token, then preserved Herdr id (§7), unaffected by this amendment.
+requirements:
+- B1: preserved — 1:1 holds: threads_seat stays write-once with succession admitted only against a Restore intent for a final-retired seat, and the one-non-retired-clone-per-seat invariant is unchanged (ThreadsSeatAssignment); pre-D1 precedence adds a pane-uniqueness tie-break so one pane is never bound to two clones.
+- B3: preserved — before D1 an Unresolved threads answer no longer overrides the old matcher (threads speaks only with Resolved, Retired or KeyConflict), so no matcher recovery regresses before the D1-gated deletion; after D1 the unseated case is covered by key-reservation resolve plus the resume driver.
+- B4: preserved — restarts stay unattended: the resume driver's restart trigger now also covers a clone unseated at restart (threads_seat = None with a recorded reservation, after D1), whose seat the resolve want then learns from ReserveContinuityKey's seat; the stale key-conflict alert can no longer block relaunch (launch is gated on current SeatStatus).
+- B5: preserved — live handoff uses the same SeatObservation path (Resolved at the same pane) and resume driver; unchanged by the amendment apart from the precedence and alert rules above.
+- B6: preserved — the key reaches the agent with no Herdr change: the adapter types `export K=V` into the pane shell (pane.send_text/send_keys) before agent.start, which Herdr v0.9.5 runs as typed input in that same shell, so the agent inherits it.
+- B7: preserved — retirement stays immediate (SeatObservation retires on close) and undoable: graph undo writes a Restore intent, reopens the tab, un-retires (D2) or succeeds (pre-D2 / operator-final) the seat from that intent, and the resume driver resumes the session; SeatObservation no longer re-retires the restoring clone, so undo completes.
+- B8: preserved — agent exit with the pane open changes nothing here: the seat stays Resolved, no trigger fires, memberships stay.
+- B9: preserved — the continuity key is still launcher-supplied cooperative evidence, now delivered by shell export; emitted only once reserved.
+- B10: preserved — after D2 undo un-retires the same seat (UnretireSeat, driven by the Restore intent), and threads restores the memberships it kept while reversible, with no re-acceptance; the finalize tombstone guarantees FinalizeRetirement eventually runs at purge, so a reversible seat does not linger with memberships after its undo window.
